  "authoringNote": "The final encounter and final order state the same date. Only the encounter states an explicit completion time; the order states no time. C02 sequences a same-day order only when both sources state explicit times placing the order strictly after completion, and no time is inferred from a date, so the pair holds R04.same_day_unsequenced, manual_review for the administrative reviewer (SPEC R04 and F07: ambiguous case separately flagged). No order time is guessed. R04 cites the encounter status, date, completion timestamp and practitioner identifier and the order status, date and practitioner identifier (seven) and names no parent (C07). R05 compares the receipt with the order only: the order states no timestamp and 2026-09-03T17:05:00Z is after the span 2026-09-01T10:00Z to 2026-09-03T12:00Z (C06), so R05 passes with four citations and never cites the encounter time. R01, R02, R03, R07, R08 and R09 pass, R06 is qualified clinical review with five clinical citations and no administrative effect, and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_human_review.",
